# hyp_at_least.fw — hypergeometric upper-tail probability P(X >= kmin).
#
# Drawing n items WITHOUT replacement from a population of N with K successes,
# the probability of getting AT LEAST kmin successes is the tail sum of the
# PMF from kmin up to n (you can never draw more successes than items drawn):
#
#   hyp_at_least(N, K, n, kmin) = sum over k = kmin..n of hyp_pmf(N, K, n, k)
#
# The PMF term hyp_pmf(N,K,n,k) = nCr(K,k)*nCr(N-K,n-k)/nCr(N,n) is written
# inline as nested multiplicative products so the WHOLE tail is one bounded
# aggregation — the iterator k drives the upper bound of the inner nCr(K,k)
# and nCr(N-K,n-k) products. Each product stays exact (overflow-safe), so the
# tail is an exact rational up to the final divisions.
#
# (The inline form is used rather than summing cross-file hyp_pmf calls because
# bounded aggregation unrolls at load time, before a cross-file callee in the
# body could be resolved — see hyp_pmf.fw for the composing per-k PMF.)
#
# Keystone (PNF card-deck cross-check, N=54 deck, K=13 clubs, draw n=5):
#   hyp_at_least(N=54, K=13, n=5, kmin=2)  ->  0.3467505241  (P(>=2 clubs))
#
# Usage:
#   hyp_at_least(N=54, K=13, n=5, kmin=2, result=?p)

result = sum( product((K-k+i)/i, i in [1..k]) * product((N-K-(n-k)+i)/i, i in [1..n-k]) / product((N-n+i)/i, i in [1..n]), k in [kmin..n])
